# P1: the device profile of the traffic candidate c2-packed-tp4-best-ship, copying the P2/P3 conventions of tp4-profile2-jobs: status, an all-four reset and two gate arms on the SAME four real-text
# coding prompts (shapes fixed in scripts/ci/ops_profile_plan.py): ops-twin unprofiled (the per-round trace_ms, the [PACKED-*] and [PHASE] splits and the texts), ops-trace profiled (tracy, op-support
# 20000 - 200000 segfaults the dispatch thread, any other count is refused - the CPP post-process only, a read-back after every 2nd verify replay, no prefill flush).
# NEVER CANCEL this job once the gate step has started: the profiler writes as root and a cancel can leave root-owned files that break the next checkout. A segfault in
# read_core_data_from_completion_queue is INFRA: do not raise op-support. Disk: the profile tree up to 4 GB; the guard stops the arm at 4 GB or 85% disk. NEVER delete the P8 base image.
# READ: ops-trace texts equal ops-twin's; the per-op table against the earlier c2-packed-tp4-speed-strace profile (what the nine levers removed and what now leads the round).
# Duration (estimate): 130 min (80 best, 190 worst). Soft.
# A committed TEMPLATE of .github/c2-serving-job.env for the tp4/next-5 four-card development window (scripts/ci/c2_serving_job.py parses it): copy it over
# .github/c2-serving-job.env on a throwaway commit of tp4/next-5 and push a tag experiment/c2-serving-vN. Nothing here names a rig, a card, a host or a
# registry: the cards are resolved at run time. The jobs are templates only: no tag is pushed from this branch by its author.
# ONE IMAGE FOR THE WHOLE WINDOW: C2_IMAGE_TAG=tp4-next-5a is what B0 builds from the pushed tp4/next-5 commit; every later job serves that one image. A commit of a
# file the image carries needs a new B0 build and a new tag in every template. The cards are under development: this window never stops, starts or hands back the node agent.
C2_CARDS=quad
C2_ACTIONS=status reset gate
C2_IMAGE_TAG=tp4-next-5a
C2_PROFILE=c2-packed-tp4-best-ship
C2_GATE_PLAN=ops-twin,ops-trace
C2_GATE_JIT=record
